An aligned altar means one that's to one of the three gods of your
class's pantheon, i.e. not to Moloch.  It's like an aligned priest.  A
*co*aligned altar is to your god, and that's what you're looking for,
as opposed to a *cross*aligned altar, i.e. one to one of the other two.
 I think there's some key you can press that'll tell you who the altar
is to, like | or something, but I personally don't mess with it; I just
drop a food ration (or whatever) on the altar, step off, and step back
on again and my character notes the alignment of the altar.  This has
never caused me any trouble, simply because if my character is already
running around on the Astral Plane (s)he usually isn't going to have
trouble waiting an extra 4 moves at each altar, and if anything, might
be able to use the heal-up time if I didn't buff up enough before the
Run.

